  bootwright / controller install
      Prepare this host's context-independent controller prerequisites: the baseline host
      packages, installed through the host's own dnf, and the controller runtime, a venv on the
      OS Python holding exactly the wheels this build locks. This command selects no context;
      the prerequisites a context adds are installed by the controller stage of apply. A ready
      host makes no request and no change. Otherwise the plan shows dnf's own preview before
      confirmation. --dry-run never elevates: it names the host package requirements without a
      preview and makes no changes, and --dry-run --output json or --output yaml also lists
      every locked wheel's file, URL and SHA-256. --wheel-mirror reads each locked wheel as
      <mirror>/<filename> from a file:/// directory or an HTTPS base, as untrusted transport:
      the lock's SHA-256 alone decides whether the bytes are used. --download-only --dest-dir
      DIR never elevates and changes only DIR: on any connected host it writes the locked
      wheels of every Python ABI, the pip wheel and a copy of lock.json, so DIR serves an
      offline host as a --wheel-mirror. Review the plan before confirming; --yes skips ordinary
      confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright controller install [flags]

  Command flags
      --dest-dir       Write the locked wheels, the pip wheel and lock.json into this directory
                       (requires --download-only)
      --download-only  Write the locked files for an offline host and change nothing else;
                       never elevates
      --dry-run        Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --wheel-mirror   Read each locked wheel as <mirror>/<filename>: file:///<directory> or
                       https://<host>/<base>; its bytes must still match the lock
      --yes            Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright controller install --dry-run
